        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is grade 2 knee osteoarthritis serious?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Grades 1 and 2 are both routinely described as mild, and most grade 2 knees do not deteriorate quickly. In an eight-year follow-up of knees graded 1 to 3, 85.7% stayed on a stable trajectory with about 0.5mm of joint space lost in total. Grade 2 is, however, the stage at which narrowing appears to move fastest, at around 0.35mm per year, so it is a sensible point to start exercise and weight management rather than to wait." } },
