        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does grade 4 osteoarthritis always need a knee replacement?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Joint replacement is considered for severe symptoms after non-surgical treatment has been tried properly, and the decision rests on how much the knee limits your life rather than on the grade. A 2020 analysis of grade 4 knees found that 23.5% and 31.2% of people in two Korean cohorts reported no knee pain at all, alongside 5.9% in an American cohort. Your surgeon decides this with you, not from the film alone." } },
